<title>GREECE: ATHLETICS-FREEMAN WINS WORLD WOMEN'S 400 METRES TITLE.</title>
<headline>ATHLETICS-FREEMAN WINS WORLD WOMEN'S 400 METRES TITLE.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Cathy Freeman won the women's 400 metres gold medal on the third day of the world championships on Monday.</p>
<p>Sandie Richards of Jamaica took the silver and American Jearl Miles-Clark the bronze.</p>
</text>
